{"kind":"artifact","text":"docs/reference/gs/status.md at f83d5cd52d7588abc78d716c157d53056cd36d12 on request/commitment-honesty.\n\nThe page documents what gs status shows and how it partitions commitments, and this branch changed that partition. It now rests on internal/statusview, which owns the lane classification, and on internal/workroom, which produces the statuses being classified.\n\nIts previous anchor named a documentation-set commit rather than either package whose behaviour the page describes, so changing the lanes could not flare it. internal/statusview had no artifact at any commit until this branch, which is why pages describing the lanes were anchored to whatever else was to hand.\n\nThe attention lane now names released and revoked alongside stale, reneged and cancelled. Both are third-party retirements and both are deliberately non-terminal, because terminal rows are dropped from the bounded lists and an authority removing work that was not theirs is exactly the row a reader needs to see.","body":{"branch":"request/commitment-honesty","commit":"f83d5cd52d7588abc78d716c157d53056cd36d12","head":"f83d5cd52d7588abc78d716c157d53056cd36d12","path":"docs/reference/gs/status.md"}}